-    <h3>Exact identity</h3>
+    <details><summary>Exact identity</summary><div class="detail-body">
     <p>A settlement matches only when all identity dimensions agree: network passphrase, sender, recipient,
       asset type, asset code and issuer (case-sensitive for credit assets), and the time window. An
       <code>operation_id</code> disambiguates multiple payments inside a single transaction. A token contract
       address is never an issuer alias.</p>
 
-    <h3>Amounts</h3>
+</div></details>
+    <details><summary>Amounts</summary><div class="detail-body">
     <p>Values are exact stroop integers within the signed int64 range, including at the limit. Inputs with
       excess precision fail validation; amounts are never rounded and no monetary tolerance is applied.</p>
 
-    <h3>Time windows</h3>
+</div></details>
+    <details><summary>Time windows</summary><div class="detail-body">
     <p>A record supplies <b>exactly one</b> representation: a legacy <code>timestamp</code> or an explicit
       <code>settlement_start</code>/<code>settlement_end</code> interval. Intervals are closed and are not
       widened by time tolerance; they must fit the reconciliation window. A partially intersecting interval is
       reported, never silently filtered. <code>business_reference</code> is separate from
       <code>reference_id</code>, which means the transaction hash only — never a memo.</p>
 
